the same namespace-on-a-specialization difference, here for std::initializer_list itself: cxx1 writes V?$initializer_list@H@@ where cl writes V?$initializer_list@H@std@@, and the constructor and begin/end that carry it differ with it. Templates are keyed by their bare name, so a specialization does not know which namespace it came from; docs/CONFORMANCE.md records it. cl also emits its own compiler-known initializer_list where cxx1 builds against include/initializer_list. What this case is about, a class template's initializer_list constructor being emitted rather than left undefined at link, is checked by run-cases.cmd on the box and run.sh on the other two.
